    sampleAnswer: 'Infinite re-render loops occur when code inside a component triggers a state update during render, either directly or via an immediately invoked effect. Common causes: 1) Calling `setState` directly in the render body or writing `onClick={doAction()}` (invoking immediately during JSX evaluation); 2) A `useEffect` that updates state while having dependencies that change on every render (e.g., an unmemoized object `deps: [{ filter }]` where `{ filter }` is a new object reference every render). To debug: check the console stack trace, inspect component render triggers via React DevTools Profiler, and eliminate cyclic dependencies by memoizing objects (`useMemo`), using primitive dependencies, or using functional state updates (`setVal(p => ...)`).',
